\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.02622222222222,322.68148148148146 77.84786516853933,308.3820224719101 130.18729729729728,268.8648648648649 200.3355844155844,207.0909090909091 278.1696103896104,235.45454545454544 360.196338028169,110.28169014084506 409.41307692307697,75.55555555555554\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 135 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.02622222222222\" cy=\"322.68148148148146\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 89 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"77.84786516853933\" cy=\"308.3820224719101\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"130.18729729729728\" cy=\"268.8648648648649\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 40%&amp;#10;It rained 48% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"200.3355844155844\" cy=\"207.0909090909091\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"278.1696103896104\" cy=\"235.45454545454544\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"360.196338028169\" cy=\"110.28169014084506\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 234 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.41307692307697\" cy=\"75.55555555555554\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(50%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Newcastle upon Tyne the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.30) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.07).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'>0.070</td><td class='num'>18.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.181</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.233</td><td class='num'>17.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>0.299</td><td class='num'>12.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":54.97328,"lon